{"authored" [{"question" "q-106464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation $(y-5)^{2}=2(x-2)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h)$ that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ are\n\n$$\nx-h=p{t}^{2},\\,y-k=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case $(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),$ we see that the parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(2,5).$ So we have\n\n$$\nx-2=p{t}^{2},\\,y-5=2pt.\n$$\n\nNow, comparing the right-hand sides of the given Cartesian equation and the general case, then solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p(x-h) & =2(x-2) \\\\ 4p(x-2) & =2(x-2) \\\\ 4p & =2 \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx-2=(\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{2},\\,y-5=2(\\frac{1}{2})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y-5=t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cb67ee7103b14ebe343eb7adab4f94f0aed04e66bb41f728230e171115f90223" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y+5=t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-5=2t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-5=t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-5=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y-2=t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106464" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-5=t,\\,\\,y-2=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx-2=-4t,\\,y-5=-2{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x-2}{4},\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{y-5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{x-2}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{y-5}{2}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16} & =-\\frac{y-5}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-8(y-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cb67ee7103b14ebe343eb7adab4f94f0aed04e66bb41f728230e171115f90223" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/state.json" "file_sha256" "f158fbc8580e7c4a3abd291244f128d5092afa92791560c306e335b2d6ba10b4" "basis" 1188 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014336/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-106502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-2)^{2}=-8(y-5)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questi